{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "title",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -950,
      "width": 1800,
      "height": 600,
      "color": "5",
      "text": "# Tack final-shape handler and display-cache flow\n\nEach row is one chronological left-to-right path. `ReplaceRhinoObject` is shown where Rhino emits it, but Tack does not subscribe to it. Runtime display data is marked dirty during replacement lifecycle events and cleaned only after final-object analysis completes."
    },
    {
      "id": "legend",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2300,
      "y": -950,
      "width": 2500,
      "height": 600,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "## Callback policy\n\n- `ReplaceRhinoObject`: not subscribed\n- `DeleteRhinoObject`: lifecycle-only; marks matching cache dirty\n- `AddRhinoObject`: installed final object; normal maintenance trigger\n- `UndeleteRhinoObject`: restored final object; Undo/Redo maintenance trigger\n- `DrawForeground`: reads clean runtime cache only"
    },

    {"id":"g-move","type":"group","x":0,"y":0,"width":5700,"height":1050,"color":"5","label":"1 — Move parent: final AddRhinoObject triggers correction"},
    {"id":"m-command","type":"text","x":120,"y":180,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"5","text":"## `_Move` parent\n\n```text\n_Move 0,0,0 0,10,0\n```\n\nRhino begins replacing the parent geometry."},
    {"id":"m-replace","type":"text","x":1050,"y":180,"width":620,"height":700,"text":"## `ReplaceRhinoObject`\n\n```python\n# Tack is not subscribed\n```\n\nThe transient old/new pair does not enter Tack maintenance and does not move the child."},
    {"id":"m-delete","type":"text","x":1980,"y":180,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"1","text":"## `DeleteRhinoObject`\n\n```python\nruntime.mark_object_ids_dirty(ids)\nreturn\n```\n\nThe matching display cache is hidden. No analysis runs because the final parent is not installed yet."},
    {"id":"m-add","type":"text","x":2910,"y":180,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"2","text":"## Parent `AddRhinoObject`\n\n```python\nObjectId → installed parent\nmark_display_dirty(state)\nmaintain_link(...)\n```\n\nThe callback supplies a usable final object ID and document object."},
    {"id":"m-maintain","type":"text","x":3840,"y":180,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"6","text":"## Analyze, correct, cache\n\n```python\nresult = inspect_link(final_parent, child)\nchild.Transform(correction)\nchild.CommitChanges()\nset_display_clean(parent, target_child)\n```\n\nSaved anchor metadata plus final geometry determine the correction."},
    {"id":"m-result","type":"text","x":4770,"y":180,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"4","text":"## Nested child callbacks → clean\n\nChild `ReplaceRhinoObject` is ignored. Child `DeleteRhinoObject` briefly marks dirty; child `AddRhinoObject` is skipped while `busy=True`. Parent maintenance finishes by writing the clean cache."},

    {"id":"g-undo","type":"group","x":0,"y":1200,"width":5700,"height":1050,"color":"3","label":"2 — Undo Move: UndeleteRhinoObject refreshes restored final geometry"},
    {"id":"u-command","type":"text","x":120,"y":1380,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"3","text":"## `_Undo`\n\nRhino restores child and parent geometry through replacement lifecycle callbacks."},
    {"id":"u-replace","type":"text","x":1050,"y":1380,"width":620,"height":700,"text":"## Child `ReplaceRhinoObject`\n\n```python\n# Tack is not subscribed\n```\n\nNo old/new remapping and no correction occur here."},
    {"id":"u-delete","type":"text","x":1980,"y":1380,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"1","text":"## Child `DeleteRhinoObject`\n\nThe child cache becomes dirty and is hidden. The handler waits for an installed restored object."},
    {"id":"u-undelete","type":"text","x":2910,"y":1380,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"2","text":"## Child `UndeleteRhinoObject`\n\n```python\nrestored child → inspect_link(...)\nundo_or_redo(doc) → no correction\nset_display_clean(live anchors)\n```\n\nRhino, not Tack, restores the geometry."},
    {"id":"u-parent","type":"text","x":3840,"y":1380,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"2","text":"## Parent restoration sequence\n\n```text\nReplaceRhinoObject  ignored\nDeleteRhinoObject   dirty\nUndeleteRhinoObject inspect + clean\n```\n\nThe final parent callback refreshes the cache again from restored geometry."},
    {"id":"u-result","type":"text","x":4770,"y":1380,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"4","text":"## Restored and clean\n\nParent and child remain where Undo restored them. No Tack child transform occurs, and the conduit resumes drawing from the refreshed clean cache."},

    {"id":"g-face","type":"group","x":0,"y":2400,"width":5700,"height":1050,"color":"6","label":"3 — MoveFace: transient empty ID is irrelevant because Tack waits for AddRhinoObject"},
    {"id":"f-command","type":"text","x":120,"y":2580,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"6","text":"## `_MoveFace` parent\n\n```text\n_MoveFace 0,0,0 2,0,0\n```\n\nThe edited Brep changes the parent’s static anchor location."},
    {"id":"f-replace","type":"text","x":1050,"y":2580,"width":620,"height":700,"text":"## `ReplaceRhinoObject`\n\n`NewRhinoObject.Id` may be `Guid.Empty`, but Tack is not subscribed and does not depend on that transient ID."},
    {"id":"f-delete","type":"text","x":1980,"y":2580,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"1","text":"## `DeleteRhinoObject`\n\nThe current parent ID matches runtime state, so the display cache becomes dirty. No final-shape analysis runs."},
    {"id":"f-add","type":"text","x":2910,"y":2580,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"2","text":"## Parent `AddRhinoObject`\n\nThe installed Brep now has a usable ID and can be found through the document. Tack marks dirty and enters maintenance."},
    {"id":"f-maintain","type":"text","x":3840,"y":2580,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"6","text":"## Static final-shape analysis\n\n```python\nparent_anchor = analyzer.resolve(parent, metadata)\ntarget = parent_anchor + offset\n```\n\nTack corrects the child, persists metadata, and caches final draw points."},
    {"id":"f-result","type":"text","x":4770,"y":2580,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"4","text":"## Corrected and clean\n\nNested child callbacks are suppressed by `busy`. The conduit resumes only after parent maintenance stores the clean parent and child anchors."},

    {"id":"g-boolean","type":"group","x":0,"y":3600,"width":5700,"height":1050,"color":"1","label":"4 — Boolean Difference: AddRhinoObject adopts the new metadata-bearing parent"},
    {"id":"b-command","type":"text","x":120,"y":3780,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"1","text":"## `_BooleanDifference`\n\nThe command creates a new result object and removes the original parent."},
    {"id":"b-add","type":"text","x":1050,"y":3780,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"2","text":"## Result `AddRhinoObject`\n\nObserved order begins with Add. The new object carries copied parent-link metadata and has a usable installed ID."},
    {"id":"b-adopt","type":"text","x":1980,"y":3780,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"2","text":"## Adopt final candidate\n\n```python\nrole = candidate_role(state, result)\nreplacement_anchor(result, saved_anchor)\nstate[\"parent_id\"] = result.Id\n```\n\nNo old/new geometry pair is required."},
    {"id":"b-maintain","type":"text","x":2910,"y":3780,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"6","text":"## Inspect and reconcile\n\nTack resolves the final parent and child anchors, applies any required correction, saves the adopted IDs, and writes a clean display cache."},
    {"id":"b-delete","type":"text","x":3840,"y":3780,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"1","text":"## Source `DeleteRhinoObject`\n\nThe runtime state already points to the new result ID. The deleted old ID no longer matches, so it does not dirty the newly cleaned cache."},
    {"id":"b-result","type":"text","x":4770,"y":3780,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"4","text":"## New parent is active\n\nPersisted metadata and runtime state reference the Boolean result. The conduit draws only the clean cached anchors produced by maintenance."},

    {"id":"g-clear","type":"group","x":0,"y":4800,"width":5700,"height":1050,"color":"1","label":"5 — commands/tack_clear.py: discard runtime cache and persisted relationships"},
    {"id":"c-command","type":"text","x":120,"y":4980,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"1","text":"## `commands/tack_clear.py`\n\nRuns against the active document when the user intentionally clears Tack relationships."},
    {"id":"c-unsubscribe","type":"text","x":1050,"y":4980,"width":620,"height":700,"text":"## Unsubscribe handlers\n\n```python\nhandlers.unsubscribe()\n```\n\nNo callbacks run while metadata and runtime state are removed."},
    {"id":"c-stop","type":"text","x":1980,"y":4980,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"3","text":"## Stop runtime\n\n```python\nconduit.Enabled = False\nsc.sticky.pop(CONDUIT_KEY)\nsc.sticky.pop(RUNTIME_KEY)\n```\n\nAll cached draw data is discarded immediately."},
    {"id":"c-metadata","type":"text","x":2910,"y":4980,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"1","text":"## Remove persisted metadata\n\n`Tack.AnchorLinks.v3` and `Tack.AnchorParentLinks.v3` are removed from document objects."},
    {"id":"c-redraw","type":"text","x":3840,"y":4980,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"4","text":"## Redraw\n\nThe disabled conduit has no runtime state to draw, so all Tack graphics disappear."},
    {"id":"c-result","type":"text","x":4770,"y":4980,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"4","text":"## Cleared\n\nNo handlers, no conduit, no runtime caches, and no persisted Tack relationships remain."},

    {"id":"g-restore","type":"group","x":0,"y":6000,"width":5700,"height":1050,"color":"2","label":"6 — commands/tack_restore.py: rebuild clean caches once, then draw without analysis"},
    {"id":"r-command","type":"text","x":120,"y":6180,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"2","text":"## `commands/tack_restore.py`\n\nReactivates Tack relationships persisted in the active document."},
    {"id":"r-reset","type":"text","x":1050,"y":6180,"width":620,"height":700,"text":"## Reset old runtime\n\n```python\nhandlers.unsubscribe()\nruntime.stop_runtime()\n```\n\nAny stale conduit and cache are removed before rebuilding."},
    {"id":"r-read","type":"text","x":1980,"y":6180,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"3","text":"## One-time metadata scan\n\n```python\nfor saved_link in metadata.all_links(doc):\n    start_runtime(..., redraw=False)\n```\n\nDocument analysis occurs during restore, not during drawing."},
    {"id":"r-cache","type":"text","x":2910,"y":6180,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"6","text":"## Build clean runtime cache\n\n`start_runtime()` resolves both anchors, stores their points and offset length, and enables the single shared conduit."},
    {"id":"r-subscribe","type":"text","x":3840,"y":6180,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"2","text":"## Subscribe + one redraw\n\n```python\nhandlers.subscribe()\ndoc.Views.Redraw()\n```\n\nAll links are restored before the one batched redraw."},
    {"id":"r-result","type":"text","x":4770,"y":6180,"width":620,"height":700,"color":"4","text":"## Restored and performant\n\nEvery valid relationship starts clean. Future viewport redraws iterate cached runtime states without metadata reads or anchor analysis."}
  ],
